```python
def lca_bst(root, p, q):
    node = root
    while node:
        if p.val < node.val and q.val < node.val:
            node = node.left
        elif p.val > node.val and q.val > node.val:
            node = node.right
        else:
            return node  # split point: this is the LCA
    return None
```

No recursion, no stack, O(1) extra space beyond the single `node` reference — a direct benefit of the BST's ordering letting you discard one entire subtree at each step, rather than needing to explore (and remember to return from) both sides the way the general-tree version does.
